.TH HTOP_PLUS 1 "2026" "htop_plus" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
htop_plus \- interactive process viewer with NVIDIA and power cable meters
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B htop_plus
.RI [ htop-options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
htop_plus extends htop with NVIDIA GPU sensors, Docker-aware process
usernames, and a read-only WINGSTUDIO 12V-2X6 Ti cable meter.
The USER column displays Docker owners as [container-name]container-user.
The NVIDIA meter shows usage, used/total VRAM in K/M/G, temperature,
fan percentage/RPM, and power in watts.
The external cable meter shows six voltage/current/power channels,
total cable power on a 1000W display scale, connector temperature (Con),
and controller temperature (Ctl).
The 1000W scale does not measure total PSU power or configure hardware limits.
.PP
Press F2 to configure meters and columns; press F10 or q to quit.
Run htop_plus --help for the full list of supported htop command-line options.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --readonly
Disable process-changing operations.
.TP
.B --version
Display the underlying htop version.
.TP
.B --help
Display all supported command-line options.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HTOPRC
Override the user interface configuration file.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
User configuration directory, defaulting to $HOME/.config.
Installed htop_plus creates htop_plus/htoprc here on first run.
Existing layouts are preserved during startup and upgrades.
.TP
.B HTOP_POWER_CABLE_CONFIG
Select another connection configuration instead of /etc/nvpowermon/config.json.
The USB serial number and optional VID/PID identify the current serial port.
.TP
.B HTOP_POWER_CABLE_PORT
Override the configured connection with an absolute /dev/ path, or set
to off to disable cable queries.
.TP
.B DOCKER_HOST
Select a local Docker socket using unix:///path/to/docker.sock.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/htop_plus/htoprc
Per-user meter layout, independent of the original htop configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/nvpowermon/config.json
Existing read-only intelligent cable connection settings.
.SH NOTES
The installer uses /usr/local by default and keeps the modified htop binary
under libexec/htop_plus. It does not replace the system htop executable.
The source checkout launcher keeps its layout in the source directory.
